            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method for video encoding, comprising: splitting a video frame into a plurality of blocks, determining whether one or more of the reference pictures associated with an inter-mode coded block involved in an operation of an inter-mode coding tool are long-term reference pictures and constraining the operation of an inter-mode coding tool on the inter-mode coded block based on the determination, wherein in the case that the inter-mode coding tool comprises Bi-Directional Optical Flow, BDOF, and the inter-mode coded block is a bi-directional prediction block, constraining the operation of the inter-mode coding tool on the inter-mode coded block based on the determination comprises: prohibiting the performance of the BDOF when determining that one reference picture of the bi-directional prediction block is a long-term reference picture and the other reference picture of the bi-directional prediction block is not a long-term reference picture.</p>
            </abstract>
